## Change (fix #2)

`runtime/main.c`, `runtime/http.h`, ring 1024 → 2048. No ABI/emitted changes.

Old SQ-full behavior: `arm_read` silently marked the conn closing (drop storm
under accept bursts at very high VU), `arm_accept` **exited the server**.
New: a deferred re-arm queue.

- `defer_arm(op, slot)` — per-conn `deferred` flag guarantees one queued entry
  max; queue capacity MAXCONN+8 (one entry per conn is structurally impossible
  to exceed; overflow closes defensively).
- `flush_deferred()` runs after each batch's final submit. A conn with a
  deferred arm has **no in-flight op** (the arm decision came from a cqe we
  just processed), so no cqe can race the re-arm; entries are revalidated
  (fd, closing, flag — conn_close clears fd, memset-on-reuse clears the flag)
  before re-arming. Flag is cleared *before* the retry so a re-full SQ
  re-queues instead of losing the arm.
- Deferred accept is retried last; the loop ends with
  `flush_deferred(); if (sq_pending) submit;` so **everything is submitted
  before every blocking wait** — a deferred accept can never sit behind a
  `min_complete=1` wait (that would deadlock the whole server).
- Ring 2048: SQ-full now needs >2048 in-flight arms vs 16384 conns; with the
  queue, even that is safe instead of fatal.

